  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Replace the Human Rights Act with a British Bill of Rights; update communications powers and add tools against non‑violent extremism; maintain strong Armed Forces, renew the nuclear deterrent, and uphold NATO; target net migration in the tens of thousands with stronger deportation, landlord checks, and English‑fluency requirements; impose an overall welfare cap, freeze most working‑age benefits, reduce the household cap, and tighten conditionality; raise the Personal Allowance and higher‑rate threshold; cut red tape and expand jobs/apprenticeships. TEXT_C: Maintain the Human Rights Act and ECHR; oppose blanket data retention; require parliamentary approval for military action; oppose renewal of the UK nuclear deterrent; restore the 50p top rate with bankers’ bonus and mansion taxes, abolish non‑dom status, uprate benefits and abolish the Bedroom Tax; increase the minimum wage and promote the living wage; expand free childcare and protect/expand welfare programmes.",
